      "dom_id": "question-176017",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-4x+5<-7$ is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+5 & <-7 \\\\ -4x+5-5 & <-7-5 \\\\ -4x+0 & <-12 \\\\ -4x & <-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-4.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,-12 \\\\ \\frac{-4x}{-4}\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{-12}{-4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-4}x}{\\cancel{-4}}\\, & >\\,\\,3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & >\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>3.$",
